{
  "method_label": "Method 3: Corridor-aware backbone\u2013feeder construction",
  "method_description": "Method 3 extends the manually guided backbone\u2013feeder network by treating intermediate waypoint cities along hub-backbone corridors as corridor access anchors. These anchors are not full fixed hubs, but they allow nearby terminals to feed into the nearest trunk corridor instead of being routed all the way to the nearest fixed hub. This is intended to reduce competing radial spokes and to produce a cleaner trunk-and-branch rail network. Phoenix remains a fixed Southwest hub, Los Angeles\u2013San Antonio is split through Phoenix, and hub-backbone corridors are manually guided through selected major cities. Key West is removed from the terminal set.",
